# Shell scripts must keep LF endings whatever the checkout platform does.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with `core.autocrlf=true`, which rewrites
# LF to CRLF on checkout. A shell script that reaches a Linux host with CRLF
# endings fails at the shebang — the kernel reads the interpreter as
# "/usr/bin/env bash\r", which does not exist, and reports
# "bad interpreter: No such file or directory". The scripts here are meant to
# be uploaded to Hostinger and run over SSH, so that is not hypothetical.
*.sh text eol=lf
